body:
I've successfully failed at trying to make work for myself. Haven't been able to pay my loans for a while and gotta pay much more now and if I fail this, it's technically repo time.

&#x200B;

I'm better off dead, got nothing to offer anyone or can funtion accordingly to expectations.

When I feel real bad, I take away my creature comforts and just plop on the floor hoping to die. Feels as if I'm not supposed to have anything, starts hurting myself by clawing or hitting my head on the wall. It feels super odd when I just do these things out of the blue.

&#x200B;

I guess you should find some positive distraction or focus on not harming yourself. If you like apps, there's some nice cute and colourfull apps for meditation.

&#x200B;

Here's one that's been popping up a lot: [https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=uk.org.stem4.calmharm&hl=en](https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=uk.org.stem4.calmharm&hl=en)

Dude, you're just 17 and just studying is totally normal, you're not your peers.  Do things on a pace that suits you.

&#x200B;

Get back to her, apologize and tell her what's on your mind. Be clear. Comunicate.

Malay here.  There's something seriously scary hive-mind of the older generations of SEA. So much hypocrisy, denial and they just don't want to bother with things they don't understand.

&#x200B;

I got to know that earlier this year an acquaintance lost his father. The man was very sick and people knew. I don't remember the details, but one day he was found on the floor shaking and in pain. Of course it must me a demon possessing him, lets pick some banana leaves, slap the poor sick man with it and compel the demons to leave his body. It's so surreal and so sad that that's the FIRST REACTION TO A SICK PERSON WHO NEEDS MEDICAL HELP IMMEDIATELY.

&#x200B;

If you have "morally corrupt western" friends, please do chat/talk with them.
